<title>UK: Bankers Trust sets warrants on the MIB 30 index.</title>
<headline>Bankers Trust sets warrants on the MIB 30 index.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bankers Trust International said it has issued two million call and put knock-out with rebate warrants, in two equal tranches, on the MIB 30 index.</p>
<p>COMMON TERMS:</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	06.NOV.97		 PAYDATE	26.NOV.96</p>
<p> LISTING	   LUXEMBOURG		MIN EXER LOT 100</p>
<p> EACH WARRANT CONTROLS ONE INDEX.</p>
<p>* * * * * *</p>
<p> WARRANT     EXERCISE	 ISSUE</p>
<p> CALL*	 15641.85	 738.88 LIRE</p>
<p> PUT**	 14152.15	 570.97 LIRE</p>
<p>* FOR THE CALL ONCE THE INDEX REACHES A LEVEL OF 18621.25</p>
<p>THEN PAYOFF WILL BE FIXED AT A LEVEL EQUAL TO 1489.70</p>
<p>**FOR THE PUT ONCE THE INDEX REACHES A LEVEL OF 11172.75,</p>
<p>PAYOFF WILL BE FIXED AT A LEVEL EQUAL TO 1489.70.</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
